From 2fa48553ce108ad7f4c2d9ccdd94e13ef6d03418 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 10:33:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0351 -- DOSAGS_RELEASE: a release flavour
 without the timing instrumentation

`make DOSAGS_RELEASE=1` (-DDOSAGS_RELEASE, build/ags-release) compiles out: every
tick-timing scope, manual bracket and record (dos_port_tick_timing.h: constant-false
fine test, empty scope); the 0230 work-vector snapshots, per-tick loops and lines; the
stallwhat and skipframe attribution; the per-call brackets for script file I/O, object
setup, screenshots and 8-bit fade steps; the periodic rbstruct / dirtypresent / bgstruct /
biggui lines; the quit-time phase aggregates and counter dump; the DOSAGS_TICKSTATS_FINE,
DOSAGS_TICKLOG, DOSAGS_FLIP_INSTR and DOSAGS_CLOCK_CROSSCHECK reads.

It keeps RUNMANIFEST and every line the gate scorers and the DOSBox-X ratchet read: the
0093 yardstick (DosTickStallScope's two clock reads per tick: tick_rate_steady, stalls,
fps_basis, and the per-second "DOS-PORT persec" series), tick_rate / frames_skipped, build_dirty, audio_vital_status and the
silentirq / startlat lines, journeys and room_transition, presentverify (env), the freeze
instrument (env), the stress and break hooks (env), and every functional kill switch.
The work-vector counters are still incremented (integer adds on hot paths), but in this
flavour nothing reads them: the "work scope=" and "workpersec" lines are compiled out with the
snapshots. Compiling out the increments too changes the release exe and is left for a later
patch with its own ratchet run.

Release only, operator 2026-11-04: DOSAGS_FIXED_TIMESTEP defaults on (every gate cell ran
with it); DOSAGS_FIXED_TIMESTEP=0 turns it off.

The instrumented flavour is unchanged: its clean-build exe differs from af3f0824499e's in 13
bytes, all of them the binary_sha12 stamp's characters (four movl immediates, the last one
overlapping the third); build_dirty does not differ.
